# An `extern` group in each of two modules of a ring, panel 252's R1
# (2026-11-19): `xa` binds `xa.h` and its C record `XRect`, which `xb` takes
# from it, and `xb` binds `xb.h`. Each module calls its own header through a
# function of its own, since an `extern` called from another module is
# `extern_across_modules` in any graph. 3 * 4 doubled, plus 1 + 2, is 27.
use xa

function main()
    print(xa.run())
